"""tomato-bazel mdBook theme — the tomato brand applied to docs, via brando.

`@tomato_brand//mdbook:theme` is an mdBook `theme/` overlay generated by brando's
brand_mdbook_theme from the tomato palette (tomato red + Bazel-leaf green calyx) +
Space Grotesk faces + the canonical v2 mark as favicon. A pure static filegroup
(no toolchain deps), so any repo consumes it as its theme dir; pair with book.toml:

    [output.html]
    additional-css = ["theme/css/custom.css"]

Used by tomato-bazel/docs (tbzl.dev) via rules_tomato's tomato_mdbook(theme = ...).
"""

load("@brando//:defs.bzl", "brand_mdbook_theme")

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

# brando 0.2.0 uses the LEGACY `colors` path here, on purpose: tomato-bazel/brand
# is the one brand repo with NO skins/ directory at all, so there is no
# meridian.theme.v1 Theme to derive from. The token names are now the schema's
# roles rather than fastverk's nicknames (@INK@/@CREAM@/@TERTIARY@), which is why
# these moved even though the values did not.
#
# TODO: give tomato a skin. It is the only brand that cannot drive its docs, its
# brando 0.2.0: derived from //skins:tomato, the skin this repo gained in the same
# wave. The ten-entry `colors` dict that was here — itself a rename of seven
# fastverk-nicknamed attributes — was the second of three places tomato typed its
# palette. It is now typed once, in skins/tomato.textpb.
brand_mdbook_theme(
    name = "theme",
    favicon = "//gen:tomato_v2_mark_transparent.svg",
    font_family = "Space Grotesk",
    medium_ttf = "//fonts:SpaceGrotesk-Medium.ttf",
    semibold_ttf = "//fonts:SpaceGrotesk-SemiBold.ttf",
    skin = "//skins:tomato_json",
)
